    "lawCode": "Amd §11-a, Chap 415 of 1913",
    "lawSection": "Commissions",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3430\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend chapter 415 of the laws of 1913, relating to\nestablishing a state commission for the blind and visually\nhandicapped, in relation to the operation of vending facilities\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nAmendment to the mini Randolph Sheppard act of 1992, an act which\ncreated the Business Enterprise Program.  The bill seeks to increase\nemployment opportunities for members of the Business Enterprise\nProgram.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSEE BILL.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Business Enterprise Program (BEP) was established as way to\nprovide people who are visually impaired with jobs as retail facility\nmanagers in state buildings. However, due to recent government\ndown-sizing and other reasons, job opportunities for B.E.P members in\nthis regard have decreased by 25%.\n\nIn order to expand and improve job opportunities for blind vendors,\nthis measure would remove several restrictions in the original act.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2008: A.10691 Referred to Assembly Economic Development Committee\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
